  "id": "culture_romulus_remus",
  "latin": "Rōmulus et Remus",
  "english": "According to legend, Romulus and Remus were twin sons of the war god Mars. As babies they were left by the river Tiber and raised by a she-wolf. When they grew up, they decided to found a city but quarreled over where: Romulus chose the Palatine Hill, Remus the Aventine. In the best-known version of the story, Remus mocked his brother's new wall by jumping over it, and Romulus killed him in anger. Romulus then named the city Rome after himself. The Romans dated the founding to 753 BCE.",
