  "english": "Romulus is said to have marked out his city by plowing a furrow around the Palatine Hill. The sacred boundary of a Roman city became known as the pōmērium. Roman law and religion treated the space inside it differently: for example, a general's military command did not extend across it, and burials were not allowed within it. As Rome grew, the pōmērium was later moved outward.",
